le-school\", \"question_type\": \"tossups\", \"source\": \"2022 SCOP MS 11\", \"round\": \"6\", \"number\": \"3\", \"parts\": [{\"label\": \"tossup\", \"question\": \"It is not magnetism, but this property confines the plasma in a hohlraum to fuse deuterium and tritium. A balance named for this concept can measure mass in the absence of gravity. Torque is proportional to a (*) “moment” named for this concept that explains why dishes remain in place when a tablecloth is quickly pulled away. Newton’s first law concerns, for ten points, what principle that describes the tendency of objects to remain either in uniform motion or at rest?\", \"answer\": \"inertia (accept inertial)\"}]}]}}",
